   "l": "Bent, then whole;",
   "v": true,
   "n": "Six sayings follow, each of them two words with 則 between: no 'if', no subject, no tense — 'be A and you are B'. You met the frame in chapter 18 (大道廢，有仁義) without even a 則 to mark it. These six read like proverbs, and the chapter itself says at the end that they are: 古之所謂, 'what antiquity called'. The book is quoting.",
   "p": true
  },
