   "l": "Warped, then straight;",
   "v": true,
   "n": "曲 and 枉 are not the same bend. 曲 is the natural curve of something that yields — a bow, a bent arm. 枉 is a straight thing pushed crooked, and in legal language it is a wrong done to a man. English 'bent' and 'warped' keep about as much of the difference as can be kept."
