   "l": "Hollow, then filled;",
   "v": true,
   "n": "盈 has been the book's image for the fullness that spoils itself — chapter 9's 持而盈之, chapter 15's 夫唯不盈. Here it is the reward, because the hollow is where water goes. Nothing in the line says water; the reader of the period did not need telling."
