   "v": true,
   "i": "Keep to little, and something comes to you; take on much, and you are lost among it.",
   "n": "得 and 惑 rhymed when this was composed — both belong to the same Old Chinese rhyme group, and both ended in the same consonant. Mandarin dé and huò keep nothing of it. This is the usual case in the book, and the reason a translation cannot show you the verse: chapter 1's 妙 / 徼 was the lucky exception."
