   "l": "Therefore the sage holds the One in his arms and is the model for all under heaven.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "So the sage keeps his arms about the One, and becomes the pattern for all under heaven.",
   "n": "抱一 is the phrase chapter 10 opened with (載營魄抱一): holding the undivided, the Way before anything has been told apart from anything. 式 is a workshop word — the form a thing is made to, the standard the others are cut against — and its being here is the point: the sage is not a ruler who issues the pattern but the pattern itself."
